@hevmind @LightOnIO For the dense model, only the languages we translated for achieve okay performance (and the results are somewhat uniform)

For the late interaction models, almost all the languages performs very well, even outside of the training languages/scripts
However, as noted in BP/paper, there are a few OOD languages such as Yoruba that are weaker than the others (compared to models that trained for it), most likely because the base backbone is weaker on those!

